  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "S1 requires reporting all thermal incidents (24h serious, 30d other) and prompt customer notice. S2 sets a 5% failure limit but allows continued sale under corrective plans with no fixed stop, and keeps per-model results from public publication. S3 requires new-unit shut-off immediately and installed-unit retrofit/equivalent within 72 months; S4 requires built-in suppression at 36 months; S5 mandates per-model recall at 8/100k with no corrective alternative and prompt notices."
